<%#
  Every Gerber layer, drill file, .gbrjob and zipped export anywhere in the folder, grouped into
  boards and each one rendered as a stackup — the private partial's shape (projects/_fabrication.html.erb) with
  public URLs, the arrangement public/projects/_schematics.html.erb already uses.

  THE GROUPING IS THE SAME SERVICE (Maker::GerberSets, reached through pub.gerber_boards), so a
  board is the same thing on both pages. What differs is only where the bytes come from.

  NO PER-ROW `permits?`: the rows come from the listing, every one of which is a live, visible file
  beneath the project folder — which IS the ancestry arm of permits? (Maker::PublicProject#bundle_files
  makes the identical argument at length). The token rides along on every URL through
  `file_url_for`, so an unlisted project's links keep working.

  THE LIST LINKS ARE `download: true` FOR THE SCHEMATICS PARTIAL'S REASON: a .gbr is not an
  inline-safe type, so the delivery concern would attach it anyway, and there is no private file
  page to send a visitor to instead. The VIEWER's own URLs are not — it fetches them with `fetch`
  and reads the text, and ?download=1 would only add a Content-Disposition nothing reads.

  THE VIEWER'S LIST IS FilesHelper#gerber_layers_for, not `stacked` spelled out here: a zipped
  export is one entry carrying the ZIP's own URL and the member paths the browser extracts with
  JSZip (Maker::GerberArchive), and that shape is defined once for this partial, the private one
  and the file page.

  Local: pub (Maker::PublicProject).
%>
<% if pub.gerber_boards.any? %>
  <section class="panel fabrication-panel">
    <h2>Fabrication</h2>
    <% pub.gerber_boards.each do |board| %>
      <div class="fabrication-board">
        <h3><%= board.name %></h3>
        <ul class="schematics-list">
          <% board.rows.each do |row| %>
            <li>
              <%= link_to row.node.name, pub.file_url_for(row.node_id, download: true) %>
              <span class="badge"><%= gerber_layer_label(row.node.name) %></span>
            </li>
          <% end %>
        </ul>
        <div class="gerber-stage"
             data-controller="gerber"
             data-gerber-single-value="false"
             data-gerber-layers-value="<%= gerber_layers_for(board) { |row|
                   pub.file_url_for(row.node_id, filename: row.node.name) }.to_json %>">
          <p class="muted" data-gerber-target="status">Loading the viewer…</p>
          <p class="gerber-sides">
            <button type="button" class="btn small active" data-gerber-target="side"
                    data-gerber-side="top" data-action="gerber#top">Top</button>
            <button type="button" class="btn small" data-gerber-target="side"
                    data-gerber-side="bottom" data-action="gerber#bottom">Bottom</button>
          </p>
          <div data-gerber-target="stage"></div>
        </div>
      </div>
    <% end %>
  </section>
<% end %>
